# Normalize line endings so every platform builds byte-identical frontends.
# Vite content-hashes the output — a CRLF checkout on Windows produced
# different asset hashes than Linux/macOS (caught by the CI verify gate in
# v1.4.11). LF everywhere keeps the packages identical.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-specific scripts keep CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.wasm binary
*.zip binary
*.jks binary
